+// Encodes `bitmap` as a PNG and writes it to `path`, both off the UI thread,
+// so a capture never stalls the frames it is measuring. `fast` trades file
+// size for encode time.
+void EncodeAndWritePng(SkBitmap bitmap, base::FilePath path, bool fast);
+
+// Handles `record DIR MS [SCALE]`: copies every frame `widget` draws for MS
+// milliseconds to DIR/fNNNN.png, scaled by SCALE (default 1), and writes one
+// JSON line per frame to DIR/frames.jsonl, then a "done" line. Recording
+// keeps the compositor drawing, so time idle frames with the frame log
+// instead. Returns false if `words` isn't a record request.
+bool HandleRecordRequest(views::Widget* widget,
+                         const std::vector<std::string>& words);
+
